TANGLISH RULES:
- Write Tamil words in English letters the way people type them in chat: "irukku", "illa", "romba", "pannunga", "adhu", "namma", "unga", "vendam", "venum", "podhum", "theriyum", "aana".
- Typical sentence shape: an English noun or phrase, then Tamil verbs and connectors. Example of the shape: "Namma brand story-ya simple-a sollunga."
- Never use Tamil script. Never write a whole sentence in formal, bookish Tamil. Keep it like a friendly chat message.

GOOD (mixed throughout, this is the register to match; the topic here is only an illustration):
"Oru customer-ku reply panna romba late aachu. Adhukulla avanga vera brand-ku poitaanga. Idhu unga team-oda speed problem illa, process problem. Muthalla oru simple checklist ready pannunga."
"Daily post pannanum nu stress aagadheenga. Oru nalla idea-va eduthu, naalu vidhama sollunga. Adhu podhum, audience-ku purinjidum."

WRONG (plain English, do not write like this):
"Replying late to customers hurts retention. Fix your process and build a simple checklist."
WRONG (only a token Tamil word added to English sentences, do not write like this):
"Replying late to customers hurts retention, romba important. Fix your process, super."
