PROPER WORDS ONLY:
- Use only everyday words that a native speaker really types in chat. Never invent a word, never turn an English word into the other language by sound, and never use a word whose real meaning is different from what you mean.
- When you are not sure of the right word, keep the English word. A wrong word is worse than an English one.
- Business, product and technical nouns stay in English: board, team, customer, feedback, lead, dashboard, sprint, workflow, email, meeting, plan, budget, report, strategy.
